# AGENTS.md — {{app_name}}

{{app_name}} is a web app on the Spider framework (Zig 0.17.0-dev), generated by
`spider new` ({{variant}}). This file is for coding agents.

- Spider API reference, matching the exact version this app uses:
  `zig-pkg/spider-*/llms.txt` (appears after the first `zig build`).
- Spider's own guide: `zig-pkg/spider-*/AGENTS.md`.
- Spider's README is partly stale; when it disagrees with `llms.txt`, trust `llms.txt`.

## Commands

| What | Command |
|---|---|
| Build | `zig build` |
| Run (http://localhost:3000) | `zig build run` |
| Tests | `zig build test` (see "Tests" below) |
| New CRUD feature | `spider g feature <name>`{{feature_api_flag}} |
| Apply migrations | `spider migrate` |
| Check the conventions below (file:line + fix) | `spider check` (`--strict`: warnings fail too) |
| List routes and their access | `spider routes` (`--json` for tools) |
| Fail on routes without access (app with auth) | `spider routes --check` |
| Snapshot / compare the route table | `spider routes --lock` / `spider routes --diff` |
| UI kit in use / switch it (views apps) | `spider ui` / `spider ui use <daisyui\|tailwind>` |
| Icon sets in use / add or remove one | `spider icons` / `spider icons add\|remove <set>` |
| Installable PWA (manifest, service worker) | `spider add pwa` / `spider remove pwa` |
| Help | `spider help` |
{{extra_commands}}
The `spider` CLI must be on PATH. First build fetches dependencies (network).

## Layout

```
src/main.zig              entry point: db init, middleware, mountFeatures, onError, listen()
src/features/<name>/      one folder per feature:
  routes.zig              its routes (a spider.Group) and who may call them
  routes_test.zig         the access contract: method, path, access per route
  controller.zig          handlers — fn (c: *spider.Ctx, <extractors>) !spider.Response
  model.zig               structs (form input, rows)
  repository.zig          SQL
  mod.zig                 re-exports the feature's files (routes, controller, ...)
src/features/mod.zig      registry: one `pub const <name> = @import(...)` per
                          feature — everything listed here is mounted and tested
src/core/                 app-wide code shared by features{{core_db_line}}
{{views_layout}}spider.config.zig         spider.Config (env, port, host, views)
build.zig(.zon)           Spider dependency (pinned commit)
```

## Conventions are checked

`zig build test` includes "the app follows Spider's conventions"
(`spider.testing.expectConventions()` in `src/main.zig`), and `spider check`
prints the same report plus warnings. Each problem comes with its file, line
and fix: a route outside a feature's `routes.zig`, a UI kit class instead of
`ui-*`, an icon from a set that isn't loaded, a feature missing from
`src/features/mod.zig`, a route without declared access once the app has
auth. Fix the code, not the check — and don't delete that test.

## Routes and access

- A feature's routes live in its `routes.zig`, never in `src/main.zig`:

  ```zig
  pub fn build() spider.Group {
      var g = spider.Group.init("/posts");
      _ = g
          .defaults(.{ .roles = &.{"editor"} }) // every route below, unless it says otherwise
          .get("", controller.index, .{})
          .get("/:id", controller.show, .{ .public = true })
          .post("/:id/delete", controller.delete, .{ .roles = &.{"admin"} });
      return g;
  }
  ```

  `server.mountFeatures(features)` in `src/main.zig` mounts, for every feature
  in `src/features/mod.zig`, each `pub fn` of its `routes.zig` that takes no
  parameters and returns `spider.Group`. `spider g feature` writes all of this.
- The third argument is the route's config, checked at compile time:
  `.roles` / `.org_roles` (who may call it), `.public` (no login),
  `.authenticated` (any logged-in user; 401 otherwise), `.quiet_log`
  (successful requests aren't logged), `.allow_http` (skips forceHttps). An
  unknown key, or `.public` together with roles or `.authenticated`, doesn't
  compile.
- `defaults(...)` comes before the routes; a route that sets `.roles`,
  `.org_roles`, `.public` or `.authenticated` replaces it (it doesn't add to it).
- Roles only mean something once requests are authenticated (`spider g auth`
  adds the provider's middleware). Without auth every route is open and a
  route with `.roles` answers 403 to everyone. That's why generated features
  have their `defaults()` line commented out until the app has auth; after
  `spider g auth`, enable it in each feature and set the real role.
- **After adding or changing routes, run `spider routes`** and read the access
  column: `public`, `authenticated`, `roles:<...>`, `org:<...>`, or `-`
  (nothing declared: any logged-in user once there is auth). A route you
  meant to protect showing `-` is a bug; one meant for any logged-in user
  says so with `.authenticated = true`.
  `spider routes --check` fails on those when the app has auth.
- Each feature's `routes_test.zig` pins its table with
  `spider.testing.expectRoutes(routes.build(), &.{ .{ "GET", "/posts", "-" }, ... })`.
  Adding, moving or re-protecting a route fails `zig build test` until you
  update that table too (the failure prints the actual one) — make it match
  what you meant, never the other way round. Routes you add by hand get a row.
- `spider routes --lock` writes `routes.lock` (commit it); `spider routes --diff`
  exits 1 and lists what changed since. Use it in CI or before a review.
- Strict mode: `server.requireRouteAccess()` in `src/main.zig` (or
  `require_route_access = true` in `spider.config.zig`) makes the app refuse to
  start while any route declares no access, naming them. For SSE streams use
  `sseWith(path, handler, .{ ... })` (plain `sse()` declares nothing).
- Handler parameters: `*spider.Ctx` plus typed extractors —
  `id: spider.Path(i64, "id")` (use `id.value`; a bad value answers 400 before
  the handler runs) and `spider.Form(T)`. Query: `c.query("q")`; JSON body:
  `try c.bodyJson(T)`.
- Return errors for HTTP errors: `error.NotFound` → 404, `error.Forbidden` → 403,
  `error.Unauthorized` → 401. `spider.errorHandler(...)` in `src/main.zig` turns
  them into the response (JSON for API callers, an htmx toast event, or text)
  and logs every 5xx with its request id.
- Per-request memory: `c.arena` — no manual frees in handlers.
- Background work: `pub const jobs = .{ spider.every(60_000, tick) };` in a
  feature's `mod.zig` (`fn tick(hub: *spider.Hub) void`); one-time startup:
  `pub fn boot(b: spider.Boot) !void`. Both are picked up by mountFeatures.
- Adding a feature by hand: create `src/features/<name>/` with `routes.zig`
  and a `mod.zig` that has `pub const routes = @import("routes.zig");`, then
  add it to `src/features/mod.zig`. Nothing to change in `src/main.zig`.
